# Trust anchor for release signature verification (Makefile: release-alpha,
# the default RELEASE_ALLOWED_SIGNERS).
#
# git allowed-signers format. The release commit's author e-mail must be a
# principal on a line here, and the commit and tags must verify against that
# line's key. It is deliberately IN-REPO and never derived from RELEASE_GIT: a
# caller-supplied helper could otherwise ship its own keypair and place a
# matching public key where the recipe looked, and forge a release that
# verified against the attacker key. Changing this file is a reviewed change,
# which is what makes it an anchor at all.
#
# Public half of the key agent-go-quicraft signs with; the private half lives
# only in the company repo (infra/gitea/agent-keys/, mode 600).
agent-go-quicraft@example.internal ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIO4zYciUPVq8P1993g/mgQgDndTE2gOcxS7iRPO/9LhM agent-go-quicraft@example.internal
